---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="About" description="What raylib-zig is, who made raylib, and the licenses involved.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      raylib-zig is a port of <a href="https://www.raylib.com">raylib</a> from C to Zig. It is an independent,
      unofficial project. It is not raylib.com, and the raylib project does not maintain it.
    </p>

    <h2>raylib</h2>
    <p>
      raylib is a library for making games and graphics programs. It is created by Ramon Santamaria
      (<a href="https://github.com/raysan5">@raysan5</a>) and many contributors. Its design is what this port keeps:
      the same functions, the same names, the same behaviour.
    </p>

    <h2>The examples</h2>
    <p>
      Every example on this site is one of raylib's own. The C source is shown unchanged, with its original author and
      license. The Zig version is a translation made for raylib-zig.
    </p>

    <h2>Licenses</h2>
    <p>
      raylib and its examples are licensed under the zlib/libpng license. raylib-zig keeps that license and the
      original copyright notices.
    </p>

    <h2>Source</h2>
    <p>
      The port: <a href="https://github.com/algorisys-oss/raylib-zig-port">algorisys-oss/raylib-zig-port</a>.
      This site: <a href="https://github.com/algorisys-oss/raylib-zig-web">algorisys-oss/raylib-zig-web</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
